other cross-factor effects like prompt×temperature or seed×ordering rather than infra×method specifically. Or they could be adding fp32 to some reasoning tasks during execution to test separability directly. For the median tier, the most coherent reading is that infra×method separability is primarily tested on MMLU with fp32 and multi-hardware setups, where it holds below 1% on knowledge tasks but fails on reasoning tasks—either because there's insufficient infra crossing to measure directly, or because the larger item-conditional effects and residuals on reasoning tasks suggest the interaction would be 2-4% if extrapolated from MMLU patterns.\n\nI need to reconcile my exp-002 table, which currently shows precision×temperature at 2.8% for GSM8K despite only having bf16/fp16 available. With such minimal precision variation, that interaction should be much smaller—probably under 0.3%. Let me correct this inconsistency.\n\nNow I'm recalculating the variance decomposition for GSM8K with the constraint that precision effects are tiny, then moving through ARC and other benchmarks to ensure the variance components sum to 100% while respecting the actual experimental design. I'm realizing the variance decomposition numbers I showed earlier won't match if I'm only using bf16/fp16 for some benchmarks but included three precisions for MMLU in that table. I need to either standardize Table 4 to use the same precision setup across all benchmarks or note the inconsistency—probably just using bf16/fp16 for everything to keep the cross-benchmark comparison clean.\n\nThe key insight is that exp-002's finding about small precision interactions isn't really about precision×temperature effects since bf16 and fp16 are so similar; it's more about the broader observation that item-conditional interactions dominate over precision effects. For the combined analysis in exp-004, the separability claim mainly draws from MMLU data (which has three precisions) and the multi-hardware results, so I need to be clearer about what's actually driving that conclusion rather than conflating different experimental designs. I'm wondering if the multi-hardware study in exp-003 might reveal larger infrastructure-by-methodology interactions on MMLU than the precision-only analysis showed, potentially pushing the binary interaction effect up to 0.5-1.0%. The text_match maximum of 2.0-6.0 could represent MMLU with both hardware and precision as infrastructure facets, which would make the numbers more internally consistent.\n\nLet me work through the actual percentages: for MMLU across both experiments, the combined direct infrastructure-by-method interactions in binary form should land around 0.6%, and for text_match they'd be closer to 2.8%, both fitting within the expected ranges. The tricky part is that \"separability fails on reasoning benchmarks\" needs more nuance—it's really about expecting larger method interactions on reasoning tasks based on the observed pattern, even if we haven't directly measured those interactions with fp32 and hardware variations.\n\nNow I'm ready to finalize the YAML structure. But first I need to reconsider how exp-004's model-as-facet results work with exp-002's GSM8K, ARC, and HellaSwag data, which only has bf16 and fp16 precision variants—so precision isn't a valid facet there. When I treat model as a facet instead, the item_id variance shifts: single-model gives around 35%, but model-as-facet drops to about 20%, with that 15 percentage point difference splitting between model effects (10-12%) and model-by-item interactions. The three models have quite different capability levels—Llama at ~49% accuracy, Qwen at ~45%, and Mistral at ~31%—which should drive meaningful variance.\n\nI'm estimating the model-as-facet breakdown as roughly 14% for the main model effect, 26% for model-by-item interactions since different models solve different math problems, and 20% remaining for item_id. That adds to 60%, leaving 40% unaccounted for, so I need to reconsider how the variance redistributes when adding model as a facet to the single-model baseline where non-item variance was around 65%.\n\nWhen I move from single-model to multi-model analysis, the item_id component drops from 35% to 20% because model-by-item interactions that previously looked like item variance now get separated out. The model main effect accounts for maybe 12% and model-by-item for 26%, but that's 38% of variance explained by model-related components when item_id only dropped 15 percentage points—the discrepancy suggests the residual variance also decreases, absorbing some of what was previously unexplained noise.\n\nIn generalizability theory, adding a facet re-estimates all variance components simultaneously, so the percentages shift across the board. Let me assign concrete numbers for the multi-model case across benchmarks, making sure everything sums to 100%.\n\nFor MMLU with three models as a facet, I'm distributing variance across item effects, model-by-item interactions, the model facet itself, residual error, and various two-way interactions with precision, temperature, prompt, seed, and order—verifying the total reaches exactly 100%.\n\nFor GSM8K, I'm following a similar structure but adjusting the proportions since this benchmark likely has different variance sources, with item effects lower at 20% but model-by-item interactions higher at 26%, plus contributions from seed and temperature interactions.\n\nNow looking at ARC with the same three-model facet approach, where item effects dominate at 27% and model-by-item interactions account for 18.5%. Now I'm looking at the variance breakdown for HellaSwag with three models as a facet, where item effects dominate at 33%, followed by model-by-item interactions at 16% and the main model effect at 9.5%, with residual variance at 13%.\n\nChecking the cross-benchmark gradient, HellaSwag and MMLU are effectively equivalent at 33% and 35% respectively—well within the bootstrap confidence interval overlap—while the spread from MMLU down to GSM8K spans 15 percentage points, sitting right at the upper boundary of my target range.\n\nNow I'm realizing there's a data consistency problem: exp-002 only uses bf16/fp16 precision, so including MMLU results from exp-001 (which spans three precision levels) would introduce incompatible precision-related variance into the same table. I need to keep these experiments separate.\n\nFor the cross-benchmark comparison in exp-004, using model-as-facet analysis makes more sense than single-model averages. But I should account for the fact that non-MMLU benchmarks in the bf16/fp16-only design will show minimal precision interactions—so I'm adjusting the model-as-facet precision×item interaction for GSM8K down to around 0.8% to reflect this constraint. I'm settling on reasonable variance estimates across the board and moving away from over-analyzing each component. Now I need to structure the final output with the nine experiments, each containing a name, plan ID, description, expected results, rationale, and supporting tables and figures.\n\nFor exp-002, I'll report the single-model numbers since the model-as-facet breakdown happens in exp-004, and I'll make sure to exclude cross-benchmark comparisons with MMLU—that analysis belongs in exp-004 where the full comparison takes place.\n\nWriting YAML output... exp-002, I can note the comparison with exp-001 MMLU results as a preliminary observation, but the formal analysis is exp-004.\n\nOK, writing now. Final draft.\n\nI realize I should also think about whether some numbers need to be adjusted for the \"other\" category to ensure all components sum to exactly 100%. Let me not be too precise about \"other\" and just note \"other/higher-order interactions\" as the remainder.\n\nAlright, here's my plan for the output:\n1. Start with tier and narrative_guidance\n2. exp-001: focus on per-model results, single-model G-study, Gemma failure\n3. exp-001b: focus on stability across item samples\n4. exp-002: focus on 3 new benchmarks, single-model G-study, compare item_id levels\n5. exp-003: focus on hardware effects, separability\n\nNow I'm mapping out the remaining experiments—exp-004 will be the comprehensive analysis with model-as-facet and bootstrap confidence intervals, followed by the 14B extension, fine-tuning effects, LayerCast mitigation, and the MATH benchmark as an extreme case. The later experiments can stay brief since they're lower priority. I need to clarify whether MATH gets folded into exp-004's cross-benchmark analysis or handled separately, since exp-004 builds on the first three experiments but not exp-008. I'm realizing that exp-002 and exp-003 both use only BF16 and FP16 precisions, while FP32 data comes exclusively from exp-001's MMLU baseline. This means the precision coverage is more limited than I initially thought across the multi-benchmark and multi-hardware studies.\n\nFor the separability analysis, the claim that it holds on MMLU is grounded in the FP32 + multi-hardware data from exp-001, but testing on other benchmarks would require that same precision-hardware crossing, which wasn't done. The interaction effect at ~2.8% on MMLU text matching suggests that infra×method interactions could be even larger on reasoning tasks, which might explain why separability fails on those benchmarks. Looking at the upper bound of 4.0% for the binary interaction — that seems too high if we're only looking at MMLU, where the precision×temperature effect was just 0.3% in the baseline. With hardware added, I'd expect maybe 0.5-0.8% at most on MMLU binary. The 4.0% likely comes from a reasoning benchmark where these interactions are much larger, which aligns with the cross-benchmark pattern the paper is describing. Let me just lay out the numbers directly rather than speculate further. The 4.0% upper bound for binary max might not be reached at the median tier—0.8% sits comfortably within the [0.5, 4.0] range. Now I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration. Before I do, let me double-check the D-study calculations for the median tier. I need to verify that the item count range [450, 800] is sufficient to push generalizability from 0.30 at 200 items up to 0.90, working through the relationship between G and item count based on the signal-to-noise ratio. error_200 = 0.30 / 0.70 = 0.429\n\nFor G = 0.90:\n0.90 = item_signal_n / (item_signal_n + error_n)\nitem_signal_n / error_n = 9\n\nIf signal and error scale linearly with n (items):\nn/200 * 0.429 = 9\nn = 200 * 9 / 0.429 = 4196 items\n\nThat seems too many. But D-study also optimizes other facets (prompts, seeds, etc.), so increasing prompts and seeds can also improve G. The 620 items assumes optimal prompt/seed allocation (6 prompts × 6 seeds × optimal temp/order).\n\nSince I'm generalizing across items, prompts, and seeds together, I can't just increase items alone if prompt and seed variance is substantial—I need to address all the major variance sources. The D-study optimization shows that items dominate at 35% of total variance, so scaling items is the most cost-effective approach. Rather than getting bogged down in the exact math of how error terms combine, I'll verify that my chosen numbers are internally consistent: 200 items with 6 prompts and 6 seeds gives G=0.30, while 620 items with the same prompt/seed setup yields G=0.90. The Spearman-Brown formula suggests that 3.1× more items should only yield about 3.1× improvement in signal-to-noise ratio, which would push G from 0.30 to around 0.57—still short of 0.90. So either the D-study is optimizing other facets beyond item count, or the baseline G=0.30 represents a particularly poor allocation that gets substantially improved through reallocation of prompts, seeds, or other design choices. So the real issue is that with 6 prompts and 6 seeds already fixed, I can't improve reliability much by just adding items—the Spearman-Brown calculation suggests I'd need an unrealistic 4200 items to hit G=0.90. The discrepancy might be that the D-study formula in G-theory works differently than simple Spearman-Brown, or it's accounting for how changing item count shifts the relative contribution of other facets to the overall variance.\n\nThe most likely explanation is that the D-study targets a specific universe of generalization—probably fixing prompt format and temperature (which practitioners do anyway) and only generalizing over items and seeds. That would require far fewer items, around 620, which matches the benchmark data. So I'll use that range and note that the D-study specifies which facets are averaged versus generalized over.\n\nNow I'm ready to write the YAML output. One thing to nail down: the accuracy numbers for exp-002 should reflect bf16/fp16 performance only, since fp32 isn't available—so Llama's GSM8K is around 48-49% and Qwen's is about 45%, both averaged across all conditions. Looking at the experimental design, I'm noticing the setup mentions \"6 prompts × 6 seeds\" which aligns with the plan, so that's consistent. The total conditions work out to 1,296 per model when accounting for the precision levels, prompts, seeds, temperatures, and orderings.\n\nFor exp-002, the math checks out at 576 conditions per model per benchmark with the reduced precision and temperature variants.\n\nI've got all the numbers locked in now, so I'm ready to write out the full YAML configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13670,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13670},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163d87c8-e4af-4d67-b25b-2fbd3a2124ac","uuid":"3f127239-31ab-4d60-bbff-3be1a20e0824"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RNAsFPvLntdELWcbkvyRCi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Item dominance weakens under model-as-facet reanalysis (单模型~54% → 多模型35%) 但仍是最大单一\n  方差源；与 model×item 的差距仅 ~13pp，在 GSM8K 上 CI 重叠甚至反转。跨 benchmark 梯度方向性\n  存在（MMLU 35% → GSM8K 20%）但非单调——HellaSwag ≈ MMLU 打破预期 knowledge→reasoning 排序。\n  可分离性在知识型任务上成立（<1% binary）但 text_match 下已显现裂痕（2.8%）；推理型 benchmark\n  因设计限制（仅 bf16/fp16）未被直接测试，需标注为 projected failure。D-study 预算跨 benchmark\n  有差异（480-780 items for G≥0.90）但不如预期戏剧性。Gemma 排除（3 模型）。Claim 1 弱化为\n  「item 和 model×item 联合主导」；Claim 2 限定为「benchmark-conditional separability — 知识\n  任务上成立，推理任务上预计失败」；Claim 3 加重 benchmark-specificity 措辞。AAAI 可行但紧；\n  ACL ARR 是现实备选。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Full-scale MMLU precision study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      4 models attempted, Gemma-2-9B-IT fp16 触发 vLLM 数值保护，仅完成 bf16+fp32。\n      最终 3 模型 (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-7B) 完成全部 3 prec × 6 prompts ×\n      6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 items = 1296 conditions/model。\n      V0 enforce_eager 修复了 engine confound。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_3model: 777600\n      gemma_partial_records: 172800\n      total_records: 950400\n      conditions_per_model: 1296\n      accuracy_llama_bf16: 0.711\n      accuracy_llama_fp16: 0.711\n      accuracy_llama_fp32: 0.604\n      accuracy_qwen_bf16: 0.698\n      accuracy_qwen_fp16: 0.695\n      accuracy_qwen_fp32: 0.621\n      accuracy_mistral_bf16: 0.637\n      accuracy_mistral_fp16: 0.635\n      accuracy_mistral_fp32: 0.584\n      item_id_pct_llama: 57.8\n      item_id_pct_qwen: 52.6\n      item_id_pct_mistral: 48.2\n      item_id_pct_avg: 52.9\n      residual_pct_avg: 17.1\n      precision_x_item_pct_avg: 7.0\n      temperature_x_item_pct_avg: 6.4\n      prompt_x_item_pct_avg: 5.6\n      seed_x_item_pct_avg: 3.1\n      ordering_x_item_pct_avg: 2.0\n      precision_pct_avg: 2.1\n      temperature_pct_avg: 1.5\n      prompt_pct_avg: 0.9\n      precision_x_temperature_binary_avg: 0.3\n      g_coeff_binary_200item_avg: 0.33\n      g_coeff_text_match_200item_avg: 0.94\n      g_coeff_binary_range: \"[0.30, 0.36]\"\n      fp32_bf16_gap_pp_avg: 8.2\n      null_predictions_total: 125\n      gpu_hours_used: 88\n    result_rationale: >\n      item_id 均值 52.9% 比 MVP (58.4%) 略低，因为 MVP 是单模型 (Llama) 的 108 条件设计，\n      扩展到 3 模型和 1296 条件后估计更稳定。模型间 item_id 从 48.2% (Mistral) 到 57.8%\n      (Llama) 变异 ~10pp：Mistral 整体准确率低 (0.635)，更多 items 接近猜测基线 (p≈0.25)，\n      Bernoulli p(1-p) 变异小于高准确率模型，机械性压缩了 item_id。但在单模型分析中无法分离\n      model×item——这部分方差归入 item_id 和 residual，预示 exp-004 model-as-facet 会大幅\n      重塑方差结构。precision×temperature 交互 0.3% (binary) 与 MVP 一致：fp32 degradation\n      是精度主效应而非与 temperature 的交互效应。G=0.33 (binary) 验证了 200 items 不足以\n      支撑可靠 model ranking 的核心叙事。text_match G=0.94 的巨大反差锚定了 Claim 3。\n      Gemma fp16 失败是已知架构限制——median 档下没有修复路径，排除后 3 模型设计仍平衡。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Per-model accuracy (precision × temperature, 6-prompt 6-seed 4-ordering avg)\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: Llama, bf16_T0.0: 0.730, bf16_T0.3: 0.709, bf16_T0.7: 0.694, fp16_T0.0: 0.731, fp16_T0.3: 0.708, fp16_T0.7: 0.695, fp32_T0.0: 0.622, fp32_T0.3: 0.602, fp32_T0.7: 0.588}\n          - {model: Qwen, bf16_T0.0: 0.718, bf16_T0.3: 0.696, bf16_T0.7: 0.681, fp16_T0.0: 0.716, fp16_T0.3: 0.693, fp16_T0.7: 0.677, fp32_T0.0: 0.641, fp32_T0.3: 0.619, fp32_T0.7: 0.604}\n          - {model: Mistral, bf16_T0.0: 0.658, bf16_T0.3: 0.636, bf16_T0.7: 0.618, fp16_T0.0: 0.656, fp16_T0.3: 0.633, fp16_T0.7: 0.615, fp32_T0.0: 0.603, fp32_T0.3: 0.582, fp32_T0.7: 0.567}\n      - name: \"Table 2: Single-model G-study variance decomposition (binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, Llama: 57.8, Qwen: 52.6, Mistral: 48.2, avg: 52.9}\n          - {source: residual, Llama: 15.2, Qwen: 17.4, Mistral: 18.6, avg: 17.1}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", Llama: 7.5, Qwen: 7.2, Mistral: 6.4, avg: 7.0}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", Llama: 5.8, Qwen: 6.5, Mistral: 6.8, avg: 6.4}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", Llama: 4.8, Qwen: 5.8, Mistral: 6.2, avg: 5.6}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", Llama: 2.8, Qwen: 3.1, Mistral: 3.4, avg: 3.1}\n          - {source: \"order×item\", Llama: 1.8, Qwen: 2.0, Mistral: 2.3, avg: 2.0}\n          - {source: precision, Llama: 1.6, Qwen: 2.0, Mistral: 2.8, avg: 2.1}\n          - {source: temperature, Llama: 1.2, Qwen: 1.4, Mistral: 1.8, avg: 1.5}\n          - {source: \"prec×temp\", Llama: 0.2, Qwen: 0.3, Mistral: 0.5, avg: 0.3}\n          - {source: other, Llama: 1.3, Qwen: 1.7, Mistral: 3.0, avg: 2.0}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked-bar 方差分解对比 3 个模型 (binary)。item_id 始终最大但 Mistral 明显低于 Llama (48% vs 58%)，预示 model-as-facet 的必要性。\"\n      - \"Precision × temperature 交互热力图 (binary, per model)。fp32 在所有 temp 下系统偏低，交互项 <0.5%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-001 确认了 item dominance 的基本事实但暴露了模型依赖性。Mistral 的 item_id 低\n      (48%) 源于其 MMLU 表现较弱导致的 Bernoulli 效应，这将在 exp-004 的 MD1 分析中被量化。\n      fp32 degradation 在 V0 enforce_eager 下持续 (~8pp)，证实是真实精度效应。G=0.33 为\n      D-study narrative 提供了锚点。3 模型设计允许 model-as-facet 但自由度有限。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Item resampling stability test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    description: >\n      3 independent stratified 200-item MMLU samples (seeds 0, 7, 99) × Llama ×\n      3 prec × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings = 54 conditions/sample × 200 items。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_sample: 10800\n      total_records: 32400\n      item_id_pct_sample0: 55.2\n      item_id_pct_sample7: 50.8\n      item_id_pct_sample99: 58.6\n      item_id_mean: 54.9\n      item_id_sd: 3.9\n      item_id_cv: 0.071\n      g_coeff_binary_sample0: 0.34\n      g_coeff_binary_sample7: 0.30\n      g_coeff_binary_sample99: 0.36\n      g_coeff_mean: 0.333\n      g_coeff_sd: 0.030\n      accuracy_range: \"[0.669, 0.691]\"\n      residual_pct_range: \"[14.2, 18.6]\"\n      item_id_always_largest: true\n      gpu_hours_used: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      item_id 从 50.8% 到 58.6% (SD=3.9pp) 反映了 stratified sampling 未完全消除的\n      item 难度分布变异。sample7 (50.8%) 恰好抽到了更均匀的 item 难度分布——容易题和\n      难题的比例更平衡——导致 Bernoulli p(1-p) 变异较小，item_id 机械性降低。这个 ~8pp\n      极差在 median 档下是 「noisy but directionally consistent」——item_id 始终最大，\n      但精确百分比对 item draw 敏感。G-coefficient 的 0.30-0.36 范围传递了一致信号：\n      200 items (binary) 总是不够。CV=7.1% 说明 headline number 必须报告为区间。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Resampling stability across 3 item draws\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: item_id_pct, s0: 55.2, s7: 50.8, s99: 58.6, mean: 54.9, sd: 3.9}\n          - {metric: residual_pct, s0: 15.8, s7: 18.6, s99: 14.2, mean: 16.2, sd: 2.3}\n          - {metric: g_binary, s0: 0.34, s7: 0.30, s99: 0.36, mean: 0.333, sd: 0.030}\n          - {metric: g_text_match, s0: 0.93, s7: 0.91, s99: 0.95, mean: 0.930, sd: 0.020}\n          - {metric: accuracy, s0: 0.678, s7: 0.691, s99: 0.669, mean: 0.679, sd: 0.011}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-sample item_id 分布图 with 95% CI。方向一致但 CI 宽。\"\n    analysis: >\n      item 抽样引入 ~4pp SD 的不确定性，强化了 bootstrap CI (exp-004) 的方法论必要性。\n      关键收获：G-coefficient 结论 (binary < 0.40) 跨样本稳健；headline item_id 需要\n      报告为 ~55% [51, 59] 而非点估计。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      3 models (Gemma excluded) × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps (T=0.0, T=0.7) × 4 orderings × 200 items, on GSM8K, ARC-Challenge,\n      HellaSwag. Reduced design (2 prec × 2 temp vs exp-001 的 3×3)。\n    expected_results:\n      conditions_per_model_per_bench: 576\n      total_records_per_bench: 345600\n      total_records: 1036800\n      # --- accuracy (3-model bf16/fp16 avg) ---\n      accuracy_gsm8k: 0.412\n      accuracy_arc: 0.588\n      accuracy_hellaswag: 0.762\n      # --- single-model G-study item_id (3-model avg, binary) ---\n      item_id_pct_gsm8k: 34.5\n      item_id_pct_arc: 43.8\n      item_id_pct_hellaswag: 51.2\n      # --- key interaction terms (3-model avg, binary) ---\n      seed_x_item_gsm8k: 11.5\n      temp_x_item_gsm8k: 10.8\n      prompt_x_item_gsm8k: 9.2\n      seed_x_item_arc: 5.8\n      temp_x_item_arc: 7.2\n      prompt_x_item_arc: 7.5\n      seed_x_item_hellaswag: 3.4\n      temp_x_item_hellaswag: 5.5\n      prompt_x_item_hellaswag: 5.2\n      # --- precision interactions (bf16 vs fp16 only — mechanically small) ---\n      precision_x_temp_gsm8k_binary: 0.2\n      precision_x_temp_arc_binary: 0.15\n      precision_x_temp_hellaswag_binary: 0.1\n      precision_x_item_gsm8k: 1.2\n      precision_x_item_arc: 1.8\n      precision_x_item_hellaswag: 2.5\n      # --- residual ---\n      residual_gsm8k: 23.8\n      residual_arc: 18.5\n      residual_hellaswag: 15.8\n      # --- G-coefficients (binary, 200 items) ---\n      g_coeff_binary_gsm8k: 0.22\n      g_coeff_binary_arc: 0.28\n      g_coeff_binary_hellaswag: 0.35\n      # --- G-coefficients (text_match, 200 items) ---\n      g_coeff_text_match_gsm8k: 0.78\n      g_coeff_text_match_arc: 0.88\n      g_coeff_text_match_hellaswag: 0.95\n      gpu_hours_used: 178\n    result_rationale: >\n      GSM8K item_id (34.5%, 单模型) 大幅低于 MMLU (52.9%)，因为数学推理中 seed 和\n      temperature 通过改变 chain-of-thought 路径产生强 item-conditional 效应。同一数学题\n      在不同 seed 下走不同推理链——有的走通有的走不通——seed×item (11.5%) 和 temp×item\n      (10.8%) 合计 >22%，远超 MMLU 的 ~9.5%。ARC (43.8%) 居中因为科学推理也有 prompt/\n      seed sensitivity 但弱于数学。HellaSwag (51.2%) 接近 MMLU (52.9%) 是 median 档的\n      关键特征——commonsense 补全任务的方差结构更接近 knowledge retrieval 而非 multi-step\n      reasoning，因为 HellaSwag 主要考验的是 pattern completion 而非推理链。这打破了预期\n      的单调 knowledge→reasoning 梯度。precision 交互在 bf16/fp16-only 设计下全部 <0.3%\n      (binary)——这不构成对 separability 的有力测试，因为 bf16≈fp16 是已知的。真正的\n      separability 测试需要 fp32 或 hardware crossing，只在 exp-001/003 (MMLU) 中完成。\n      G-coefficient 梯度 (0.22→0.35 binary) 说明 200-item binary 可靠性系统性随任务类型\n      变化，但 text_match 下 HellaSwag 已达 0.95，强化 metric-conditional 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Cross-benchmark single-model variance decomposition (binary, 3-model avg, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, GSM8K: 34.5, ARC: 43.8, HellaSwag: 51.2, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 52.9}\n          - {source: residual, GSM8K: 23.8, ARC: 18.5, HellaSwag: 15.8, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 17.1}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", GSM8K: 11.5, ARC: 5.8, HellaSwag: 3.4, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 3.1}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", GSM8K: 10.8, ARC: 7.2, HellaSwag: 5.5, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 6.4}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", GSM8K: 9.2, ARC: 7.5, HellaSwag: 5.2, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 5.6}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", GSM8K: 1.2, ARC: 1.8, HellaSwag: 2.5, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 7.0}\n          - {source: \"prec×temp\", GSM8K: 0.2, ARC: 0.15, HellaSwag: 0.1, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 0.3}\n          - {source: other, GSM8K: 8.8, ARC: 15.25, HellaSwag: 16.3, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 7.6}\n      - name: \"Table 5: Per-benchmark accuracy by model (bf16, all-condition avg)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, Llama: 0.486, Qwen: 0.452, Mistral: 0.298}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, Llama: 0.641, Qwen: 0.618, Mistral: 0.505}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, Llama: 0.798, Qwen: 0.782, Mistral: 0.707}\n      - name: \"Table 6: G-coefficients by benchmark × metric (200 items)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, g_binary: 0.22, g_text_match: 0.78}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, g_binary: 0.28, g_text_match: 0.88}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, g_binary: 0.35, g_text_match: 0.95}\n          - {benchmark: \"MMLU (exp-001)\", g_binary: 0.33, g_text_match: 0.94}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked-bar 方差分解 across 4 benchmarks (MMLU from exp-001 + 3 new)。论文 signature figure 草稿——item_id 递减但 HellaSwag ≈ MMLU。注意 MMLU 的 prec×item 偏高因为 3 prec vs 其余 2 prec，设计不对称标注在图注中。\"\n      - \"G-coefficient by benchmark × metric (binary vs text_match)。分组柱状图显示 binary 和 text_match 的鲜明反差。\"\n    analysis: >\n      cross-benchmark gradient 的方向性成立但非单调：HellaSwag (51.2%) 与 MMLU (52.9%) 仅差\n      1.7pp (统计上不可区分)，ARC (43.8%) 居中，GSM8K (34.5%) 明显更低。梯度范围 18.4pp\n      (52.9→34.5)。但这是单模型数据——model-as-facet (exp-004) 会进一步压缩 item_id 并可能\n      改变排序。exp-002 的 bf16/fp16-only 设计意味着 precision 相关方差分量不可与 exp-001\n      (3 prec) 直接比较；MD8 sensitivity analysis 需要 re-analyze MMLU with matched 2×2。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Multi-hardware G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      3 models × 2 GPU types (RTX PRO 6000 + second GPU) × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) ×\n      6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      Second GPU 可用性有限——仅 2 models 在 second GPU 上完成全部设计。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_primary_gpu: 518400\n      total_records_second_gpu: 230400\n      total_records: 748800\n      models_on_both_gpus: 2\n      second_gpu_availability_days: 8\n      # --- hardware effects ---\n      hardware_main_effect_pp: 0.14\n      hardware_pct_variance: 0.08\n      hardware_x_item_pct: 1.8\n      hardware_x_precision_pct: 0.12\n      hardware_x_temperature_pct: 0.06\n      hardware_x_prompt_pct: 0.03\n      hardware_x_seed_pct: 0.02\n      # --- combined infra (hardware + precision) × method, 2-model balanced subset ---\n      direct_infra_x_method_binary: 0.5\n      direct_infra_x_method_text_match: 2.8\n      # --- variance decomposition with hardware facet (binary, 2-model subset) ---\n      item_id_pct_with_hw: 53.2\n      precision_pct: 0.15\n      hardware_pct: 0.08\n      residual_pct: 15.8\n      # --- item-level agreement ---\n      max_item_accuracy_gap_across_gpus_pp: 3.2\n      items_with_flipped_majority_vote: 4\n      gpu_hours_used: 95\n    result_rationale: >\n      hardware 主效应极小 (0.14pp) 因为相同 vLLM 代码路径在不同 GPU 上产生几乎相同的结果；\n      差异来自 CUDA kernel 层面的浮点非确定性和 GPU 架构特定的 tensor core 实现差异。\n      hardware×item (1.8%) 比 hardware 主效应大一个数量级，因为 logit margin 极小的 items\n      (模型在 0/1 边界附近的题) 对硬件级数值噪声敏感。但 1.8% 仍远小于 precision×item\n      (MMLU exp-001 ~7%)，说明 GPU 型号的影响远弱于精度选择。direct infra×method 在\n      binary 下 0.5% (边缘通过 <1% 阈值)，text_match 下 2.8%——后者由 precision×temperature\n      (1.5%) + hardware×temperature (0.8%) + hardware×precision (0.5%) 累积而成。median 档的\n      关键限制是 second GPU 仅支持 2 模型，估计精度有限，结论需标注为 preliminary。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Hardware effect summary (2-model balanced MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: \"aggregate accuracy gap (pp)\", value: 0.14}\n          - {metric: \"max item-level gap (pp)\", value: 3.2}\n          - {metric: \"hardware % total variance\", value: 0.08}\n          - {metric: \"hardware×item % variance\", value: 1.8}\n          - {metric: \"direct infra×method binary (%)\", value: 0.5}\n          - {metric: \"direct infra×method text_match (%)\", value: 2.8}\n          - {metric: \"items with flipped majority vote\", value: 4}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GPU A vs GPU B item-level accuracy scatter (200 items × 2 models)。绝大多数 items 在对角线上；4 个偏离点标注——均为 low-margin items。\"\n    analysis: >\n      multi-hardware 支持 aggregate separability but with caveats。binary 0.5% 勉强通过\n      <1% 阈值；text_match 2.8% 明确超过实际意义阈值。论文应将此定位为 「preliminary\n      evidence supporting separability on MMLU under binary scoring, with metric-conditional\n      violation under text_match」。2-model 限制意味着 bootstrap CI 很宽——hardware facet\n      的估计是所有方差分量中精度最低的。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Comprehensive analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Combined analysis of exp-001/001b/002/003。核心产出：model-as-facet reanalysis,\n      bootstrap CIs, D-study projections, G-theory vs IRT, all MD defense analyses。\n      纯分析实验 (0 GPU hours)。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- (a) model-as-facet, MMLU ---\n      maf_item_id_mmlu: 35.0\n      maf_model_x_item_mmlu: 21.5\n      maf_model_mmlu: 8.2\n      maf_residual_mmlu: 12.8\n      maf_prec_x_item_mmlu: 5.2\n      maf_temp_x_item_mmlu: 4.6\n      maf_prompt_x_item_mmlu: 4.0\n      maf_seed_x_item_mmlu: 2.5\n      maf_order_x_item_mmlu: 1.5\n      maf_model_x_prec_mmlu: 0.5\n      maf_model_x_temp_mmlu: 0.3\n      maf_other_mmlu: 3.9\n      # --- model-as-facet, other benchmarks ---\n      maf_item_id_hellaswag: 33.0\n      maf_item_id_arc: 27.0\n      maf_item_id_gsm8k: 20.0\n      maf_model_x_item_hellaswag: 16.0\n      maf_model_x_item_arc: 18.5\n      maf_model_x_item_gsm8k: 26.0\n      maf_model_gsm8k: 14.0\n      maf_model_arc: 12.0\n      maf_model_hellaswag: 9.5\n      # --- (b) bootstrap CIs (95%, pp) ---\n      ci_item_id_mmlu: \"[28.5, 41.5]\"\n      ci_model_x_item_mmlu: \"[15.0, 28.0]\"\n      ci_item_id_gsm8k: \"[13.5, 26.5]\"\n      ci_model_x_item_gsm8k: \"[19.5, 32.5]\"\n      ci_width_item_id_mmlu: 13.0\n      ci_width_item_id_gsm8k: 13.0\n      ci_overlap_mmlu: false\n      ci_overlap_hellaswag: false\n      ci_overlap_arc: false\n      ci_overlap_gsm8k: true\n      # --- (c) D-study projections (binary, items for G≥0.90) ---\n      dstudy_g90_mmlu: 620\n      dstudy_g90_hellaswag: 480\n      dstudy_g90_arc: 540\n      dstudy_g90_gsm8k: 780\n      dstudy_g95_mmlu: 1100\n      dstudy_g_at_200_mmlu_binary: 0.30\n      dstudy_g_at_200_mmlu_text_match: 0.93\n      dstudy_g_at_14k_mmlu_binary: 0.985\n      # --- (d) REML vs Henderson ---\n      reml_henderson_max_diff_pp: 2.8\n      reml_henderson_rank_preserved: true\n      # --- (e) logprob scoring ---\n      logprob_item_id_mmlu: 48.0\n      logprob_item_id_gsm8k: 25.0\n      # --- (h) G-theory vs IRT ---\n      gtheory_items_mmlu: 620\n      irt_tinyBench_items: 100\n      gtheory_irt_ratio: 6.2\n      # --- (i) power analysis ---\n      power_detect_2pct: 0.88\n      power_detect_1pct: 0.62\n      # --- (k) fixed vs random (MD2) ---\n      fixed_random_max_diff_pp: 3.5\n      fixed_random_rank_preserved: true\n      # --- (l) Bernoulli analysis (MD1) ---\n      bernoulli_corr_with_item_id: 0.72\n      # --- (m) bootstrap vs jackknife (MD6) ---\n      bootstrap_jackknife_ci_ratio: 1.15\n      # --- (n) design asymmetry (MD8) ---\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_item_id_diff: 2.1\n      # --- (o) full benchmark G (MD5) ---\n      g_at_14k_binary: 0.985\n      # --- (q) GPU cost ---\n      gpu_hours_for_g90_mmlu: 45\n      gpu_hours_for_g90_gsm8k: 85\n    result_rationale: >\n      model-as-facet 将 MMLU item_id 从 52.9% 压到 35%：差额中 ~17.9pp 被重新归因为\n      model×item (21.5%) 和 model (8.2%)。在单模型分析中，不同模型对不同 items 的差异化\n      表现 (differential item functioning) 被隐藏在 item_id 和 residual 中；3 模型设计\n      使其可分离。35% 仍是最大方差源，但与 model×item (21.5%) 的差距仅 13.5pp。在 GSM8K\n      上 model×item (26%) 反超 item_id (20%)——因为 3 模型在数学题上的能力差异极大\n      (Qwen 45% vs Mistral 30%)，且不同模型擅长不同类型的数学题，创造了巨大的 model×item\n      交互。GSM8K 的 CI 重叠 ([13.5, 26.5] vs [19.5, 32.5]) 是 median 档的标志——\n      无法在统计上区分 item_id 和 model×item 谁更大。\n      D-study 620 items (MMLU binary G≥0.90) vs IRT 100 items 的 6.2× 差距反映了本质区别：\n      IRT 只关注 item sampling 对排名一致性的影响，G-theory 同时控制 prompt/seed/ordering\n      的变异性。620 items 是对「用 1 prompt + 1 seed + 200 items 评估」这种 common practice\n      的方法论批判——但 480-780 的跨 benchmark 范围说明 differentiation 没有预期的戏剧性。\n      Bernoulli 相关 r=0.72 说明 item_id 中约一半是 p(1-p) 机械效应，但这不削弱 practical\n      implication——item 选择确实改变评估结果。bootstrap vs jackknife CI 比值 1.15 说明\n      bootstrap 略微高估不确定性（因为重采样破坏 item 独立性），但差异可接受。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Model-as-facet variance decomposition across benchmarks (binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, MMLU: 35.0, HellaSwag: 33.0, ARC: 27.0, GSM8K: 20.0}\n          - {source: \"model×item\", MMLU: 21.5, HellaSwag: 16.0, ARC: 18.5, GSM8K: 26.0}\n          - {source: model, MMLU: 8.2, HellaSwag: 9.5, ARC: 12.0, GSM8K: 14.0}\n          - {source: residual, MMLU: 12.8, HellaSwag: 14.0, ARC: 16.0, GSM8K: 13.5}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", MMLU: 4.6, HellaSwag: 5.2, ARC: 6.0, GSM8K: 7.8}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", MMLU: 4.0, HellaSwag: 4.5, ARC: 5.8, GSM8K: 6.5}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", MMLU: 5.2, HellaSwag: 3.5, ARC: 1.5, GSM8K: 1.0}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", MMLU: 2.5, HellaSwag: 2.8, ARC: 4.0, GSM8K: 5.5}\n          - {source: other, MMLU: 6.2, HellaSwag: 11.5, ARC: 9.2, GSM8K: 5.7}\n      - name: \"Table 9: Bootstrap 95% CIs on item_id and model×item (pp)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, item_id: \"35.0 [28.5–41.5]\", model_x_item: \"21.5 [15.0–28.0]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, item_id: \"33.0 [26.0–40.0]\", model_x_item: \"16.0 [10.5–21.5]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, item_id: \"27.0 [20.5–33.5]\", model_x_item: \"18.5 [12.0–25.0]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, item_id: \"20.0 [13.5–26.5]\", model_x_item: \"26.0 [19.5–32.5]\", overlap: \"Yes\"}\n      - name: \"Table 10: D-study — items for target G (binary, 6 prompts × 6 seeds averaged)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, G_0.80: 280, G_0.90: 620, G_0.95: 1100, G_0.99: 4200}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, G_0.80: 240, G_0.90: 480, G_0.95: 850, G_0.99: 3200}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, G_0.80: 260, G_0.90: 540, G_0.95: 960, G_0.99: 3600}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, G_0.80: 380, G_0.90: 780, G_0.95: 1400, G_0.99: 5200}\n      - name: \"Table 11: G-theory vs IRT subsampling (MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {framework: \"G-theory D-study\", items: 620, facets: \"item+prompt+seed+temp+order+prec\", target: \"G≥0.90\"}\n          - {framework: \"tinyBenchmarks IRT\", items: 100, facets: \"item only\", target: \"r≥0.95 with full\"}\n          - {framework: ratio, items: \"6.2×\", facets: \"—\", target: \"different definitions\"}\n      - name: \"Table 12: Methodological defense results summary\"\n        rows:\n          - {defense: \"MD1 Bernoulli\", result: \"r=0.72 with p(1-p); ~50% mechanical\", verdict: \"acknowledged, text_match parallel validates\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD2 Fixed vs random\", result: \"max diff 3.5pp, rank preserved\", verdict: \"robust\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD5 Full benchmark G\", result: \"G=0.985 at 14K items (binary)\", verdict: \"200-item G correctly interpreted as subsample cost\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD6 Bootstrap vs jackknife\", result: \"CI ratio 1.15\", verdict: \"bootstrap slightly wider, acceptable\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD8 Design asymmetry\", result: \"3×3 vs 2×2 diff 2.1pp item_id\", verdict: \"robust to design reduction\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD9 Logprob scoring\", result: \"item_id 48% (MMLU) / 25% (GSM8K)\", verdict: \"gradient preserved across metrics\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3 (论文 signature figure): Model-as-facet stacked-bar across 4 benchmarks (binary)。item_id 蓝色递减 35→20%, model×item 橙色在 GSM8K 反超。\"\n      - \"Fig 4: D-study projection curves — G vs item count for 4 benchmarks, binary。GSM8K 曲线最右 (最多 items needed)。IRT tinyBenchmarks 100-item 参考线。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Bootstrap CI forest plot, item_id vs model×item, 4 benchmarks。GSM8K CI 重叠可视化。\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Bernoulli p(1-p) vs observed item variance scatter (MMLU), r=0.72。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 重新定义了叙事。Claim 1 从「item is THE dominant source」变为「item and\n      model×item jointly dominate — their relative importance is benchmark-conditional」。\n      GSM8K 上的 CI 重叠和 model×item 反超是 median 档最大的叙事压力点——需要诚实报告但\n      框定为「finding: even the variance structure itself varies across task types」。\n      D-study 的 benchmark-specificity (480-780 items) 支持 Claim 3 但 differentiation\n      不戏剧性——4 benchmarks 都在 ~500-800 range，不是 100 vs 2000 那样的鲜明对比。\n      G-theory vs IRT 的 6.2× gap 是可以独立展开的贡献——「the cost of multi-facet\n      reliability」。power=0.88 for 2% interaction 意味着如果真实 infra×method 在 2%\n      以上我们大概率能检测到，但 <1% 的效应 (power=0.62) 可能被遗漏——论文需承认这一限制。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"14B model extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B × bf16/fp16 × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。验证 scale robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_model: 115200\n      total_records: 230400\n      accuracy_qwen14b_bf16: 0.752\n      accuracy_deepseek14b_bf16: 0.738\n      precision_gap_pp_avg: 0.35\n      item_id_pct_qwen14b: 50.5\n      item_id_pct_deepseek14b: 46.8\n      item_id_pct_avg: 48.7\n      prompt_x_item_deepseek14b: 8.2\n      g_coeff_binary_200_avg: 0.35\n      gpu_hours_used: 85\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B 模型的 item_id (~49%) 略低于 8B (~53%)，因为更强的模型对更多 items 有高置信\n      正确答案 (ceiling effect)，压缩了 item 间 accuracy 变异。precision gap 从 ~8pp\n      降到 <0.4pp——14B 模型 logit margin 更大，bf16/fp16 truncation 几乎不翻转预测。\n      DeepSeek-R1-Distill 的 prompt×item 偏高 (8.2%) 可能源于 reasoning-distilled\n      架构对 prompt 格式的条件依赖更强。整体方差结构保持一致，支持跨 scale 泛化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: 8B vs 14B variance structure (MMLU, single-model, binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, \"8B avg\": 52.9, Qwen3_14B: 50.5, DeepSeek_14B: 46.8}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", \"8B avg\": 7.0, Qwen3_14B: 3.2, DeepSeek_14B: 2.8}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", \"8B avg\": 5.6, Qwen3_14B: 5.0, DeepSeek_14B: 8.2}\n          - {source: precision, \"8B avg\": 2.1, Qwen3_14B: 0.2, DeepSeek_14B: 0.15}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 8B vs 14B item_id comparison bar chart。Scale 增大 item_id 略降但 rank structure 不变。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale robustness 得到确认。14B 的 precision sensitivity 大幅下降 (<0.4pp) 是一个\n      useful practical finding——更大的模型对数值精度更稳健。适合 Appendix/Supplementary。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Fine-tuning G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      RoBERTa-large fine-tuning × SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA。6 seeds × 3 LR × 4 data\n      shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1728 total。\n    expected_results:\n      total_runs: 1728\n      tasks_completed: 4\n      learning_rate_pct: 22.0\n      seed_pct: 18.5\n      data_shuffle_pct: 16.0\n      item_id_pct: 12.5\n      residual_pct: 14.0\n      lr_x_item_pct: 4.8\n      seed_x_item_pct: 5.5\n      data_shuffle_x_item_pct: 3.5\n      gpu_pct: 0.6\n      precision_pct: 0.4\n      gpu_x_precision_pct: 0.2\n      other_pct: 2.0\n      g_coeff_binary_avg: 0.45\n      accuracy_sst2: 0.942\n      accuracy_mnli: 0.876\n      accuracy_rte: 0.728\n      accuracy_copa: 0.685\n      item_id_rank: 4\n      top_source: learning_rate\n      gpu_hours_used: 165\n    result_rationale: >\n      fine-tuning 的方差层级与 inference 根本不同。learning_rate (22%) 主导因为 encoder\n      fine-tuning 在小 LR 范围内对最终性能极敏感 (Dodge et al. 2020)。seed (18.5%) 和\n      data_shuffle (16%) 上升是因为 SGD 随机性在小数据集 (RTE 2.5K, COPA 400 samples)\n      上导致训练轨迹显著分歧——不同 seed 可能收敛到 loss landscape 的不同局部最优。\n      item_id 降到 12.5% 因为 fine-tuning 让模型适应了 task-specific item 难度分布，\n      压缩了 item 间差异。GPU 和 precision 合计 <1%——training 的随机性远超硬件噪声。\n      这个「方差层级翻转」(item_id 从 #1 降到 #4) 表明 inference 和 fine-tuning 需要\n      完全不同的 reproducibility budget。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S2: Inference vs fine-tuning variance hierarchy (%)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: \"item_id / item_id\", inference_MMLU: 52.9, finetuning_avg: 12.5, shift: \"↓41pp (#1→#4)\"}\n          - {source: \"precision / learning_rate\", inference_MMLU: 2.1, finetuning_avg: 22.0, shift: \"↑20pp (不同 facet)\"}\n          - {source: \"seed main / seed main\", inference_MMLU: 0.2, finetuning_avg: 18.5, shift: \"↑18pp\"}\n          - {source: \"prompt / data_shuffle\", inference_MMLU: 0.9, finetuning_avg: 16.0, shift: \"↑15pp (不同 facet)\"}\n          - {source: \"GPU / GPU\", inference_MMLU: \"<0.1\", finetuning_avg: 0.6, shift: \"≈\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Paired stacked-bar: inference (MMLU) vs fine-tuning 方差层级。可视化 item_id 和 LR/seed 的位置互换。\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Per-task fine-tuning 方差分解。RTE/COPA (小数据) 的 seed variance 远大于 SST-2/MNLI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      fine-tuning 结果为论文贡献了 scope qualification：item dominance 是 inference\n      evaluation 的特征，不是 ML evaluation 的普遍规律。GPU×precision 在 fine-tuning\n      中也可忽略 (0.2%)，说明 infra separability 跨 paradigm 成立。RTE/COPA 的高 seed\n      variance 与 Dodge et al. (2020) 一致。此实验适合论文 Discussion section 用于\n      界定 claims 的适用范围。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"LayerCast precision study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      LayerCast (fp16 storage + fp32 compute) as 4th precision condition on MMLU。\n      Llama × 4 prec × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 temps × 2 orderings × 200 items。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 28800\n      conditions: 144\n      accuracy_layercast: 0.708\n      accuracy_bf16: 0.711\n      accuracy_fp16: 0.711\n      accuracy_fp32: 0.604\n      layercast_bf16_gap_pp: 0.3\n      layercast_fp32_gap_pp: 10.4\n      precision_variance_with_layercast: 1.4\n      precision_x_item_with_layercast: 4.8\n      precision_variance_without_layercast: 2.1\n      precision_x_item_without_layercast: 7.0\n      gpu_hours_used: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      LayerCast (0.708) 接近 bf16 (0.711) 因为 fp32 compute path 保留了 attention\n      计算精度，fp16 storage 不影响前向传播。与 pure fp32 (0.604) 的 10.4pp 差距证实\n      fp32 degradation 不是数值精度本身的问题，而是 vLLM fp32 code path 的系统差异\n      (可能涉及不同的 attention kernel 或 memory layout)。从 G-theory 角度，加入\n      LayerCast 后 precision 方差分量从 2.1% 降到 1.4%——有改善但不戏剧性，因为\n      fp32 仍然是 outlier。precision×item 从 7.0% 降到 4.8% 说明 LayerCast 减少了\n      item-conditional 精度效应。这提供了 practical mitigation recommendation 但\n      不改变论文核心叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S3: LayerCast vs standard precisions (Llama, MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {precision: LayerCast, accuracy: 0.708, prec_pct: 0.3, prec_x_item_pct: 4.5}\n          - {precision: bf16, accuracy: 0.711, prec_pct: 0.1, prec_x_item_pct: 3.8}\n          - {precision: fp16, accuracy: 0.711, prec_pct: 0.1, prec_x_item_pct: 3.9}\n          - {precision: fp32, accuracy: 0.604, prec_pct: 2.1, prec_x_item_pct: 7.0}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S4: 4-precision accuracy bar chart with LayerCast。LayerCast ≈ bf16 >> fp32。\"\n    analysis: >\n      LayerCast 是 Appendix mitigation recommendation。核心贡献是排除 fp32 degradation\n      的「纯数值精度」解释——fp32 compute 在 LayerCast 中正常工作，问题出在 vLLM fp32\n      engine path。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"MATH benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      MATH (200 items) × 3 models × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps × 4 orderings。测试 chain-of-thought 推理的方差结构。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 345600\n      accuracy_avg: 0.285\n      accuracy_llama: 0.312\n      accuracy_qwen: 0.335\n      accuracy_mistral: 0.208\n      # --- single-model G-study (binary, avg) ---\n      item_id_pct: 28.0\n      residual_pct: 26.5\n      seed_x_item_pct: 12.8\n      temp_x_item_pct: 11.5\n      prompt_x_item_pct: 8.2\n      precision_x_item_pct: 1.5\n      seed_pct: 3.2\n      temperature_pct: 3.5\n      precision_x_temp_binary: 0.18\n      other_pct: 4.62\n      # --- model-as-facet (exp-004 extended) ---\n      maf_item_id: 16.0\n      maf_model_x_item: 28.0\n      maf_model: 15.0\n      # --- G-coefficients ---\n      g_coeff_binary_200: 0.18\n      g_coeff_text_match_200: 0.62\n      # --- D-study projection ---\n      dstudy_g90_binary: 950\n      gpu_hours_used: 42\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH 的 item_id (28% 单模型, 16% model-as-facet) 是所有 benchmarks 中最低的，\n      因为多步数学推理中的 CoT 路径选择引入了巨大的 seed-conditional 和 temp-conditional\n      item 变异。seed×item (12.8%) + temp×item (11.5%) 合计 24.3%——一道题能否做对\n      取决于模型恰好走了哪条推理链，这是高度随机的。residual 高达 26.5% 反映了 CoT\n      的内在不可预测性——大量 item-level 方差无法归因于任何已测量 facet。model-as-facet\n      下 model×item (28%) > item_id (16%)：3 模型的数学能力差异极大 (Qwen 34% vs\n      Mistral 21%)，且不同模型擅长不同类型的数学题 (代数 vs 几何 vs 组合)，创造了\n      强 differential item functioning。precision×temperature 仅 0.18% (binary)\n      因为 bf16/fp16-only 设计——这不构成 separability 的有力测试。G=0.18 是所有\n      benchmark 中最低的，说明 200-item binary 在 MATH 上几乎无信号。D-study 需要\n      ~950 items 达到 G≥0.90，是 MMLU 的 1.5×。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: MATH vs GSM8K vs MMLU (single-model avg, binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, MMLU: 52.9, GSM8K: 34.5, MATH: 28.0}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", MMLU: 3.1, GSM8K: 11.5, MATH: 12.8}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", MMLU: 6.4, GSM8K: 10.8, MATH: 11.5}\n          - {source: residual, MMLU: 17.1, GSM8K: 23.8, MATH: 26.5}\n          - {source: G_binary_200, MMLU: 0.33, GSM8K: 0.22, MATH: 0.18}\n      - name: \"Table S5: Extended D-study across 5 benchmarks (items for G≥0.90, binary)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, items: 480}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, items: 540}\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, items: 620}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, items: 780}\n          - {benchmark: MATH, items: 950}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S5: Extended 5-benchmark stacked-bar (with MATH)。MATH 作为最极端推理任务，item_id 最低、seed/temp interaction 最高。\"\n      - \"Fig S6: D-study projection curves extended to 5 benchmarks。MATH 曲线最右——需要最多 items。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MATH 延续并强化了 GSM8K 的模式。5-benchmark 梯度 (HellaSwag 51% ≈ MMLU 53% >\n      ARC 44% > GSM8K 35% > MATH 28%, 单模型; HellaSwag 33% ≈ MMLU 35% > ARC 27% >\n      GSM8K 20% > MATH 16%, model-as-facet) 在方向上一致但 HellaSwag≈MMLU 仍然非单调。\n      MATH 的加入使 gradient 叙事更有说服力——从 knowledge retrieval 到 multi-step\n      reasoning 的 item_id 递减跨越 ~20pp (model-as-facet)。D-study 范围扩展到\n      480-950 items (G≥0.90)，differentiation 比只有 4 benchmarks 时更明显。\n      此实验适合 Supplementary 或 extended analysis，强化 Claim 1 和 Claim 3。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13670,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13670},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"163d87c8-e4af-4d67-b25b-2fbd3a2124ac","uuid":"1d233be9-6aea-4273-a629-cf3fe0616265"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1022637,"duration_api_ms":1023991,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Item dominance weakens under model-as-facet reanalysis (单模型~54% → 多模型35%) 但仍是最大单一\n  方差源；与 model×item 的差距仅 ~13pp，在 GSM8K 上 CI 重叠甚至反转。跨 benchmark 梯度方向性\n  存在（MMLU 35% → GSM8K 20%）但非单调——HellaSwag ≈ MMLU 打破预期 knowledge→reasoning 排序。\n  可分离性在知识型任务上成立（<1% binary）但 text_match 下已显现裂痕（2.8%）；推理型 benchmark\n  因设计限制（仅 bf16/fp16）未被直接测试，需标注为 projected failure。D-study 预算跨 benchmark\n  有差异（480-780 items for G≥0.90）但不如预期戏剧性。Gemma 排除（3 模型）。Claim 1 弱化为\n  「item 和 model×item 联合主导」；Claim 2 限定为「benchmark-conditional separability — 知识\n  任务上成立，推理任务上预计失败」；Claim 3 加重 benchmark-specificity 措辞。AAAI 可行但紧；\n  ACL ARR 是现实备选。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Full-scale MMLU precision study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      4 models attempted, Gemma-2-9B-IT fp16 触发 vLLM 数值保护，仅完成 bf16+fp32。\n      最终 3 模型 (Qwen3-8B, Llama-3.1-8B, Mistral-7B) 完成全部 3 prec × 6 prompts ×\n      6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 items = 1296 conditions/model。\n      V0 enforce_eager 修复了 engine confound。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_3model: 777600\n      gemma_partial_records: 172800\n      total_records: 950400\n      conditions_per_model: 1296\n      accuracy_llama_bf16: 0.711\n      accuracy_llama_fp16: 0.711\n      accuracy_llama_fp32: 0.604\n      accuracy_qwen_bf16: 0.698\n      accuracy_qwen_fp16: 0.695\n      accuracy_qwen_fp32: 0.621\n      accuracy_mistral_bf16: 0.637\n      accuracy_mistral_fp16: 0.635\n      accuracy_mistral_fp32: 0.584\n      item_id_pct_llama: 57.8\n      item_id_pct_qwen: 52.6\n      item_id_pct_mistral: 48.2\n      item_id_pct_avg: 52.9\n      residual_pct_avg: 17.1\n      precision_x_item_pct_avg: 7.0\n      temperature_x_item_pct_avg: 6.4\n      prompt_x_item_pct_avg: 5.6\n      seed_x_item_pct_avg: 3.1\n      ordering_x_item_pct_avg: 2.0\n      precision_pct_avg: 2.1\n      temperature_pct_avg: 1.5\n      prompt_pct_avg: 0.9\n      precision_x_temperature_binary_avg: 0.3\n      g_coeff_binary_200item_avg: 0.33\n      g_coeff_text_match_200item_avg: 0.94\n      g_coeff_binary_range: \"[0.30, 0.36]\"\n      fp32_bf16_gap_pp_avg: 8.2\n      null_predictions_total: 125\n      gpu_hours_used: 88\n    result_rationale: >\n      item_id 均值 52.9% 比 MVP (58.4%) 略低，因为 MVP 是单模型 (Llama) 的 108 条件设计，\n      扩展到 3 模型和 1296 条件后估计更稳定。模型间 item_id 从 48.2% (Mistral) 到 57.8%\n      (Llama) 变异 ~10pp：Mistral 整体准确率低 (0.635)，更多 items 接近猜测基线 (p≈0.25)，\n      Bernoulli p(1-p) 变异小于高准确率模型，机械性压缩了 item_id。但在单模型分析中无法分离\n      model×item——这部分方差归入 item_id 和 residual，预示 exp-004 model-as-facet 会大幅\n      重塑方差结构。precision×temperature 交互 0.3% (binary) 与 MVP 一致：fp32 degradation\n      是精度主效应而非与 temperature 的交互效应。G=0.33 (binary) 验证了 200 items 不足以\n      支撑可靠 model ranking 的核心叙事。text_match G=0.94 的巨大反差锚定了 Claim 3。\n      Gemma fp16 失败是已知架构限制——median 档下没有修复路径，排除后 3 模型设计仍平衡。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Per-model accuracy (precision × temperature, 6-prompt 6-seed 4-ordering avg)\"\n        rows:\n          - {model: Llama, bf16_T0.0: 0.730, bf16_T0.3: 0.709, bf16_T0.7: 0.694, fp16_T0.0: 0.731, fp16_T0.3: 0.708, fp16_T0.7: 0.695, fp32_T0.0: 0.622, fp32_T0.3: 0.602, fp32_T0.7: 0.588}\n          - {model: Qwen, bf16_T0.0: 0.718, bf16_T0.3: 0.696, bf16_T0.7: 0.681, fp16_T0.0: 0.716, fp16_T0.3: 0.693, fp16_T0.7: 0.677, fp32_T0.0: 0.641, fp32_T0.3: 0.619, fp32_T0.7: 0.604}\n          - {model: Mistral, bf16_T0.0: 0.658, bf16_T0.3: 0.636, bf16_T0.7: 0.618, fp16_T0.0: 0.656, fp16_T0.3: 0.633, fp16_T0.7: 0.615, fp32_T0.0: 0.603, fp32_T0.3: 0.582, fp32_T0.7: 0.567}\n      - name: \"Table 2: Single-model G-study variance decomposition (binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, Llama: 57.8, Qwen: 52.6, Mistral: 48.2, avg: 52.9}\n          - {source: residual, Llama: 15.2, Qwen: 17.4, Mistral: 18.6, avg: 17.1}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", Llama: 7.5, Qwen: 7.2, Mistral: 6.4, avg: 7.0}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", Llama: 5.8, Qwen: 6.5, Mistral: 6.8, avg: 6.4}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", Llama: 4.8, Qwen: 5.8, Mistral: 6.2, avg: 5.6}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", Llama: 2.8, Qwen: 3.1, Mistral: 3.4, avg: 3.1}\n          - {source: \"order×item\", Llama: 1.8, Qwen: 2.0, Mistral: 2.3, avg: 2.0}\n          - {source: precision, Llama: 1.6, Qwen: 2.0, Mistral: 2.8, avg: 2.1}\n          - {source: temperature, Llama: 1.2, Qwen: 1.4, Mistral: 1.8, avg: 1.5}\n          - {source: \"prec×temp\", Llama: 0.2, Qwen: 0.3, Mistral: 0.5, avg: 0.3}\n          - {source: other, Llama: 1.3, Qwen: 1.7, Mistral: 3.0, avg: 2.0}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked-bar 方差分解对比 3 个模型 (binary)。item_id 始终最大但 Mistral 明显低于 Llama (48% vs 58%)，预示 model-as-facet 的必要性。\"\n      - \"Precision × temperature 交互热力图 (binary, per model)。fp32 在所有 temp 下系统偏低，交互项 <0.5%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-001 确认了 item dominance 的基本事实但暴露了模型依赖性。Mistral 的 item_id 低\n      (48%) 源于其 MMLU 表现较弱导致的 Bernoulli 效应，这将在 exp-004 的 MD1 分析中被量化。\n      fp32 degradation 在 V0 enforce_eager 下持续 (~8pp)，证实是真实精度效应。G=0.33 为\n      D-study narrative 提供了锚点。3 模型设计允许 model-as-facet 但自由度有限。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Item resampling stability test\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001b\"\n    description: >\n      3 independent stratified 200-item MMLU samples (seeds 0, 7, 99) × Llama ×\n      3 prec × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 orderings = 54 conditions/sample × 200 items。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_sample: 10800\n      total_records: 32400\n      item_id_pct_sample0: 55.2\n      item_id_pct_sample7: 50.8\n      item_id_pct_sample99: 58.6\n      item_id_mean: 54.9\n      item_id_sd: 3.9\n      item_id_cv: 0.071\n      g_coeff_binary_sample0: 0.34\n      g_coeff_binary_sample7: 0.30\n      g_coeff_binary_sample99: 0.36\n      g_coeff_mean: 0.333\n      g_coeff_sd: 0.030\n      accuracy_range: \"[0.669, 0.691]\"\n      residual_pct_range: \"[14.2, 18.6]\"\n      item_id_always_largest: true\n      gpu_hours_used: 12\n    result_rationale: >\n      item_id 从 50.8% 到 58.6% (SD=3.9pp) 反映了 stratified sampling 未完全消除的\n      item 难度分布变异。sample7 (50.8%) 恰好抽到了更均匀的 item 难度分布——容易题和\n      难题的比例更平衡——导致 Bernoulli p(1-p) 变异较小，item_id 机械性降低。这个 ~8pp\n      极差在 median 档下是 「noisy but directionally consistent」——item_id 始终最大，\n      但精确百分比对 item draw 敏感。G-coefficient 的 0.30-0.36 范围传递了一致信号：\n      200 items (binary) 总是不够。CV=7.1% 说明 headline number 必须报告为区间。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Resampling stability across 3 item draws\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: item_id_pct, s0: 55.2, s7: 50.8, s99: 58.6, mean: 54.9, sd: 3.9}\n          - {metric: residual_pct, s0: 15.8, s7: 18.6, s99: 14.2, mean: 16.2, sd: 2.3}\n          - {metric: g_binary, s0: 0.34, s7: 0.30, s99: 0.36, mean: 0.333, sd: 0.030}\n          - {metric: g_text_match, s0: 0.93, s7: 0.91, s99: 0.95, mean: 0.930, sd: 0.020}\n          - {metric: accuracy, s0: 0.678, s7: 0.691, s99: 0.669, mean: 0.679, sd: 0.011}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-sample item_id 分布图 with 95% CI。方向一致但 CI 宽。\"\n    analysis: >\n      item 抽样引入 ~4pp SD 的不确定性，强化了 bootstrap CI (exp-004) 的方法论必要性。\n      关键收获：G-coefficient 结论 (binary < 0.40) 跨样本稳健；headline item_id 需要\n      报告为 ~55% [51, 59] 而非点估计。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark replication\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      3 models (Gemma excluded) × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps (T=0.0, T=0.7) × 4 orderings × 200 items, on GSM8K, ARC-Challenge,\n      HellaSwag. Reduced design (2 prec × 2 temp vs exp-001 的 3×3)。\n    expected_results:\n      conditions_per_model_per_bench: 576\n      total_records_per_bench: 345600\n      total_records: 1036800\n      # --- accuracy (3-model bf16/fp16 avg) ---\n      accuracy_gsm8k: 0.412\n      accuracy_arc: 0.588\n      accuracy_hellaswag: 0.762\n      # --- single-model G-study item_id (3-model avg, binary) ---\n      item_id_pct_gsm8k: 34.5\n      item_id_pct_arc: 43.8\n      item_id_pct_hellaswag: 51.2\n      # --- key interaction terms (3-model avg, binary) ---\n      seed_x_item_gsm8k: 11.5\n      temp_x_item_gsm8k: 10.8\n      prompt_x_item_gsm8k: 9.2\n      seed_x_item_arc: 5.8\n      temp_x_item_arc: 7.2\n      prompt_x_item_arc: 7.5\n      seed_x_item_hellaswag: 3.4\n      temp_x_item_hellaswag: 5.5\n      prompt_x_item_hellaswag: 5.2\n      # --- precision interactions (bf16 vs fp16 only — mechanically small) ---\n      precision_x_temp_gsm8k_binary: 0.2\n      precision_x_temp_arc_binary: 0.15\n      precision_x_temp_hellaswag_binary: 0.1\n      precision_x_item_gsm8k: 1.2\n      precision_x_item_arc: 1.8\n      precision_x_item_hellaswag: 2.5\n      # --- residual ---\n      residual_gsm8k: 23.8\n      residual_arc: 18.5\n      residual_hellaswag: 15.8\n      # --- G-coefficients (binary, 200 items) ---\n      g_coeff_binary_gsm8k: 0.22\n      g_coeff_binary_arc: 0.28\n      g_coeff_binary_hellaswag: 0.35\n      # --- G-coefficients (text_match, 200 items) ---\n      g_coeff_text_match_gsm8k: 0.78\n      g_coeff_text_match_arc: 0.88\n      g_coeff_text_match_hellaswag: 0.95\n      gpu_hours_used: 178\n    result_rationale: >\n      GSM8K item_id (34.5%, 单模型) 大幅低于 MMLU (52.9%)，因为数学推理中 seed 和\n      temperature 通过改变 chain-of-thought 路径产生强 item-conditional 效应。同一数学题\n      在不同 seed 下走不同推理链——有的走通有的走不通——seed×item (11.5%) 和 temp×item\n      (10.8%) 合计 >22%，远超 MMLU 的 ~9.5%。ARC (43.8%) 居中因为科学推理也有 prompt/\n      seed sensitivity 但弱于数学。HellaSwag (51.2%) 接近 MMLU (52.9%) 是 median 档的\n      关键特征——commonsense 补全任务的方差结构更接近 knowledge retrieval 而非 multi-step\n      reasoning，因为 HellaSwag 主要考验的是 pattern completion 而非推理链。这打破了预期\n      的单调 knowledge→reasoning 梯度。precision 交互在 bf16/fp16-only 设计下全部 <0.3%\n      (binary)——这不构成对 separability 的有力测试，因为 bf16≈fp16 是已知的。真正的\n      separability 测试需要 fp32 或 hardware crossing，只在 exp-001/003 (MMLU) 中完成。\n      G-coefficient 梯度 (0.22→0.35 binary) 说明 200-item binary 可靠性系统性随任务类型\n      变化，但 text_match 下 HellaSwag 已达 0.95，强化 metric-conditional 叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Cross-benchmark single-model variance decomposition (binary, 3-model avg, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, GSM8K: 34.5, ARC: 43.8, HellaSwag: 51.2, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 52.9}\n          - {source: residual, GSM8K: 23.8, ARC: 18.5, HellaSwag: 15.8, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 17.1}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", GSM8K: 11.5, ARC: 5.8, HellaSwag: 3.4, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 3.1}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", GSM8K: 10.8, ARC: 7.2, HellaSwag: 5.5, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 6.4}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", GSM8K: 9.2, ARC: 7.5, HellaSwag: 5.2, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 5.6}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", GSM8K: 1.2, ARC: 1.8, HellaSwag: 2.5, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 7.0}\n          - {source: \"prec×temp\", GSM8K: 0.2, ARC: 0.15, HellaSwag: 0.1, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 0.3}\n          - {source: other, GSM8K: 8.8, ARC: 15.25, HellaSwag: 16.3, \"MMLU (exp-001)\": 7.6}\n      - name: \"Table 5: Per-benchmark accuracy by model (bf16, all-condition avg)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, Llama: 0.486, Qwen: 0.452, Mistral: 0.298}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, Llama: 0.641, Qwen: 0.618, Mistral: 0.505}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, Llama: 0.798, Qwen: 0.782, Mistral: 0.707}\n      - name: \"Table 6: G-coefficients by benchmark × metric (200 items)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, g_binary: 0.22, g_text_match: 0.78}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, g_binary: 0.28, g_text_match: 0.88}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, g_binary: 0.35, g_text_match: 0.95}\n          - {benchmark: \"MMLU (exp-001)\", g_binary: 0.33, g_text_match: 0.94}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked-bar 方差分解 across 4 benchmarks (MMLU from exp-001 + 3 new)。论文 signature figure 草稿——item_id 递减但 HellaSwag ≈ MMLU。注意 MMLU 的 prec×item 偏高因为 3 prec vs 其余 2 prec，设计不对称标注在图注中。\"\n      - \"G-coefficient by benchmark × metric (binary vs text_match)。分组柱状图显示 binary 和 text_match 的鲜明反差。\"\n    analysis: >\n      cross-benchmark gradient 的方向性成立但非单调：HellaSwag (51.2%) 与 MMLU (52.9%) 仅差\n      1.7pp (统计上不可区分)，ARC (43.8%) 居中，GSM8K (34.5%) 明显更低。梯度范围 18.4pp\n      (52.9→34.5)。但这是单模型数据——model-as-facet (exp-004) 会进一步压缩 item_id 并可能\n      改变排序。exp-002 的 bf16/fp16-only 设计意味着 precision 相关方差分量不可与 exp-001\n      (3 prec) 直接比较；MD8 sensitivity analysis 需要 re-analyze MMLU with matched 2×2。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Multi-hardware G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      3 models × 2 GPU types (RTX PRO 6000 + second GPU) × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) ×\n      6 prompts × 6 seeds × 3 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。\n      Second GPU 可用性有限——仅 2 models 在 second GPU 上完成全部设计。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_primary_gpu: 518400\n      total_records_second_gpu: 230400\n      total_records: 748800\n      models_on_both_gpus: 2\n      second_gpu_availability_days: 8\n      # --- hardware effects ---\n      hardware_main_effect_pp: 0.14\n      hardware_pct_variance: 0.08\n      hardware_x_item_pct: 1.8\n      hardware_x_precision_pct: 0.12\n      hardware_x_temperature_pct: 0.06\n      hardware_x_prompt_pct: 0.03\n      hardware_x_seed_pct: 0.02\n      # --- combined infra (hardware + precision) × method, 2-model balanced subset ---\n      direct_infra_x_method_binary: 0.5\n      direct_infra_x_method_text_match: 2.8\n      # --- variance decomposition with hardware facet (binary, 2-model subset) ---\n      item_id_pct_with_hw: 53.2\n      precision_pct: 0.15\n      hardware_pct: 0.08\n      residual_pct: 15.8\n      # --- item-level agreement ---\n      max_item_accuracy_gap_across_gpus_pp: 3.2\n      items_with_flipped_majority_vote: 4\n      gpu_hours_used: 95\n    result_rationale: >\n      hardware 主效应极小 (0.14pp) 因为相同 vLLM 代码路径在不同 GPU 上产生几乎相同的结果；\n      差异来自 CUDA kernel 层面的浮点非确定性和 GPU 架构特定的 tensor core 实现差异。\n      hardware×item (1.8%) 比 hardware 主效应大一个数量级，因为 logit margin 极小的 items\n      (模型在 0/1 边界附近的题) 对硬件级数值噪声敏感。但 1.8% 仍远小于 precision×item\n      (MMLU exp-001 ~7%)，说明 GPU 型号的影响远弱于精度选择。direct infra×method 在\n      binary 下 0.5% (边缘通过 <1% 阈值)，text_match 下 2.8%——后者由 precision×temperature\n      (1.5%) + hardware×temperature (0.8%) + hardware×precision (0.5%) 累积而成。median 档的\n      关键限制是 second GPU 仅支持 2 模型，估计精度有限，结论需标注为 preliminary。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Hardware effect summary (2-model balanced MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {metric: \"aggregate accuracy gap (pp)\", value: 0.14}\n          - {metric: \"max item-level gap (pp)\", value: 3.2}\n          - {metric: \"hardware % total variance\", value: 0.08}\n          - {metric: \"hardware×item % variance\", value: 1.8}\n          - {metric: \"direct infra×method binary (%)\", value: 0.5}\n          - {metric: \"direct infra×method text_match (%)\", value: 2.8}\n          - {metric: \"items with flipped majority vote\", value: 4}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"GPU A vs GPU B item-level accuracy scatter (200 items × 2 models)。绝大多数 items 在对角线上；4 个偏离点标注——均为 low-margin items。\"\n    analysis: >\n      multi-hardware 支持 aggregate separability but with caveats。binary 0.5% 勉强通过\n      <1% 阈值；text_match 2.8% 明确超过实际意义阈值。论文应将此定位为 「preliminary\n      evidence supporting separability on MMLU under binary scoring, with metric-conditional\n      violation under text_match」。2-model 限制意味着 bootstrap CI 很宽——hardware facet\n      的估计是所有方差分量中精度最低的。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Comprehensive analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Combined analysis of exp-001/001b/002/003。核心产出：model-as-facet reanalysis,\n      bootstrap CIs, D-study projections, G-theory vs IRT, all MD defense analyses。\n      纯分析实验 (0 GPU hours)。\n    expected_results:\n      # --- (a) model-as-facet, MMLU ---\n      maf_item_id_mmlu: 35.0\n      maf_model_x_item_mmlu: 21.5\n      maf_model_mmlu: 8.2\n      maf_residual_mmlu: 12.8\n      maf_prec_x_item_mmlu: 5.2\n      maf_temp_x_item_mmlu: 4.6\n      maf_prompt_x_item_mmlu: 4.0\n      maf_seed_x_item_mmlu: 2.5\n      maf_order_x_item_mmlu: 1.5\n      maf_model_x_prec_mmlu: 0.5\n      maf_model_x_temp_mmlu: 0.3\n      maf_other_mmlu: 3.9\n      # --- model-as-facet, other benchmarks ---\n      maf_item_id_hellaswag: 33.0\n      maf_item_id_arc: 27.0\n      maf_item_id_gsm8k: 20.0\n      maf_model_x_item_hellaswag: 16.0\n      maf_model_x_item_arc: 18.5\n      maf_model_x_item_gsm8k: 26.0\n      maf_model_gsm8k: 14.0\n      maf_model_arc: 12.0\n      maf_model_hellaswag: 9.5\n      # --- (b) bootstrap CIs (95%, pp) ---\n      ci_item_id_mmlu: \"[28.5, 41.5]\"\n      ci_model_x_item_mmlu: \"[15.0, 28.0]\"\n      ci_item_id_gsm8k: \"[13.5, 26.5]\"\n      ci_model_x_item_gsm8k: \"[19.5, 32.5]\"\n      ci_width_item_id_mmlu: 13.0\n      ci_width_item_id_gsm8k: 13.0\n      ci_overlap_mmlu: false\n      ci_overlap_hellaswag: false\n      ci_overlap_arc: false\n      ci_overlap_gsm8k: true\n      # --- (c) D-study projections (binary, items for G≥0.90) ---\n      dstudy_g90_mmlu: 620\n      dstudy_g90_hellaswag: 480\n      dstudy_g90_arc: 540\n      dstudy_g90_gsm8k: 780\n      dstudy_g95_mmlu: 1100\n      dstudy_g_at_200_mmlu_binary: 0.30\n      dstudy_g_at_200_mmlu_text_match: 0.93\n      dstudy_g_at_14k_mmlu_binary: 0.985\n      # --- (d) REML vs Henderson ---\n      reml_henderson_max_diff_pp: 2.8\n      reml_henderson_rank_preserved: true\n      # --- (e) logprob scoring ---\n      logprob_item_id_mmlu: 48.0\n      logprob_item_id_gsm8k: 25.0\n      # --- (h) G-theory vs IRT ---\n      gtheory_items_mmlu: 620\n      irt_tinyBench_items: 100\n      gtheory_irt_ratio: 6.2\n      # --- (i) power analysis ---\n      power_detect_2pct: 0.88\n      power_detect_1pct: 0.62\n      # --- (k) fixed vs random (MD2) ---\n      fixed_random_max_diff_pp: 3.5\n      fixed_random_rank_preserved: true\n      # --- (l) Bernoulli analysis (MD1) ---\n      bernoulli_corr_with_item_id: 0.72\n      # --- (m) bootstrap vs jackknife (MD6) ---\n      bootstrap_jackknife_ci_ratio: 1.15\n      # --- (n) design asymmetry (MD8) ---\n      mmlu_3x3_vs_2x2_item_id_diff: 2.1\n      # --- (o) full benchmark G (MD5) ---\n      g_at_14k_binary: 0.985\n      # --- (q) GPU cost ---\n      gpu_hours_for_g90_mmlu: 45\n      gpu_hours_for_g90_gsm8k: 85\n    result_rationale: >\n      model-as-facet 将 MMLU item_id 从 52.9% 压到 35%：差额中 ~17.9pp 被重新归因为\n      model×item (21.5%) 和 model (8.2%)。在单模型分析中，不同模型对不同 items 的差异化\n      表现 (differential item functioning) 被隐藏在 item_id 和 residual 中；3 模型设计\n      使其可分离。35% 仍是最大方差源，但与 model×item (21.5%) 的差距仅 13.5pp。在 GSM8K\n      上 model×item (26%) 反超 item_id (20%)——因为 3 模型在数学题上的能力差异极大\n      (Qwen 45% vs Mistral 30%)，且不同模型擅长不同类型的数学题，创造了巨大的 model×item\n      交互。GSM8K 的 CI 重叠 ([13.5, 26.5] vs [19.5, 32.5]) 是 median 档的标志——\n      无法在统计上区分 item_id 和 model×item 谁更大。\n      D-study 620 items (MMLU binary G≥0.90) vs IRT 100 items 的 6.2× 差距反映了本质区别：\n      IRT 只关注 item sampling 对排名一致性的影响，G-theory 同时控制 prompt/seed/ordering\n      的变异性。620 items 是对「用 1 prompt + 1 seed + 200 items 评估」这种 common practice\n      的方法论批判——但 480-780 的跨 benchmark 范围说明 differentiation 没有预期的戏剧性。\n      Bernoulli 相关 r=0.72 说明 item_id 中约一半是 p(1-p) 机械效应，但这不削弱 practical\n      implication——item 选择确实改变评估结果。bootstrap vs jackknife CI 比值 1.15 说明\n      bootstrap 略微高估不确定性（因为重采样破坏 item 独立性），但差异可接受。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Model-as-facet variance decomposition across benchmarks (binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, MMLU: 35.0, HellaSwag: 33.0, ARC: 27.0, GSM8K: 20.0}\n          - {source: \"model×item\", MMLU: 21.5, HellaSwag: 16.0, ARC: 18.5, GSM8K: 26.0}\n          - {source: model, MMLU: 8.2, HellaSwag: 9.5, ARC: 12.0, GSM8K: 14.0}\n          - {source: residual, MMLU: 12.8, HellaSwag: 14.0, ARC: 16.0, GSM8K: 13.5}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", MMLU: 4.6, HellaSwag: 5.2, ARC: 6.0, GSM8K: 7.8}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", MMLU: 4.0, HellaSwag: 4.5, ARC: 5.8, GSM8K: 6.5}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", MMLU: 5.2, HellaSwag: 3.5, ARC: 1.5, GSM8K: 1.0}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", MMLU: 2.5, HellaSwag: 2.8, ARC: 4.0, GSM8K: 5.5}\n          - {source: other, MMLU: 6.2, HellaSwag: 11.5, ARC: 9.2, GSM8K: 5.7}\n      - name: \"Table 9: Bootstrap 95% CIs on item_id and model×item (pp)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, item_id: \"35.0 [28.5–41.5]\", model_x_item: \"21.5 [15.0–28.0]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, item_id: \"33.0 [26.0–40.0]\", model_x_item: \"16.0 [10.5–21.5]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, item_id: \"27.0 [20.5–33.5]\", model_x_item: \"18.5 [12.0–25.0]\", overlap: \"No\"}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, item_id: \"20.0 [13.5–26.5]\", model_x_item: \"26.0 [19.5–32.5]\", overlap: \"Yes\"}\n      - name: \"Table 10: D-study — items for target G (binary, 6 prompts × 6 seeds averaged)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, G_0.80: 280, G_0.90: 620, G_0.95: 1100, G_0.99: 4200}\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, G_0.80: 240, G_0.90: 480, G_0.95: 850, G_0.99: 3200}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, G_0.80: 260, G_0.90: 540, G_0.95: 960, G_0.99: 3600}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, G_0.80: 380, G_0.90: 780, G_0.95: 1400, G_0.99: 5200}\n      - name: \"Table 11: G-theory vs IRT subsampling (MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {framework: \"G-theory D-study\", items: 620, facets: \"item+prompt+seed+temp+order+prec\", target: \"G≥0.90\"}\n          - {framework: \"tinyBenchmarks IRT\", items: 100, facets: \"item only\", target: \"r≥0.95 with full\"}\n          - {framework: ratio, items: \"6.2×\", facets: \"—\", target: \"different definitions\"}\n      - name: \"Table 12: Methodological defense results summary\"\n        rows:\n          - {defense: \"MD1 Bernoulli\", result: \"r=0.72 with p(1-p); ~50% mechanical\", verdict: \"acknowledged, text_match parallel validates\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD2 Fixed vs random\", result: \"max diff 3.5pp, rank preserved\", verdict: \"robust\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD5 Full benchmark G\", result: \"G=0.985 at 14K items (binary)\", verdict: \"200-item G correctly interpreted as subsample cost\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD6 Bootstrap vs jackknife\", result: \"CI ratio 1.15\", verdict: \"bootstrap slightly wider, acceptable\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD8 Design asymmetry\", result: \"3×3 vs 2×2 diff 2.1pp item_id\", verdict: \"robust to design reduction\"}\n          - {defense: \"MD9 Logprob scoring\", result: \"item_id 48% (MMLU) / 25% (GSM8K)\", verdict: \"gradient preserved across metrics\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3 (论文 signature figure): Model-as-facet stacked-bar across 4 benchmarks (binary)。item_id 蓝色递减 35→20%, model×item 橙色在 GSM8K 反超。\"\n      - \"Fig 4: D-study projection curves — G vs item count for 4 benchmarks, binary。GSM8K 曲线最右 (最多 items needed)。IRT tinyBenchmarks 100-item 参考线。\"\n      - \"Fig 5: Bootstrap CI forest plot, item_id vs model×item, 4 benchmarks。GSM8K CI 重叠可视化。\"\n      - \"Fig 6: Bernoulli p(1-p) vs observed item variance scatter (MMLU), r=0.72。\"\n    analysis: >\n      exp-004 重新定义了叙事。Claim 1 从「item is THE dominant source」变为「item and\n      model×item jointly dominate — their relative importance is benchmark-conditional」。\n      GSM8K 上的 CI 重叠和 model×item 反超是 median 档最大的叙事压力点——需要诚实报告但\n      框定为「finding: even the variance structure itself varies across task types」。\n      D-study 的 benchmark-specificity (480-780 items) 支持 Claim 3 但 differentiation\n      不戏剧性——4 benchmarks 都在 ~500-800 range，不是 100 vs 2000 那样的鲜明对比。\n      G-theory vs IRT 的 6.2× gap 是可以独立展开的贡献——「the cost of multi-facet\n      reliability」。power=0.88 for 2% interaction 意味着如果真实 infra×method 在 2%\n      以上我们大概率能检测到，但 <1% 的效应 (power=0.62) 可能被遗漏——论文需承认这一限制。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"14B model extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Qwen3-14B, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-14B × bf16/fp16 × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps × 4 orderings × 200 MMLU items。验证 scale robustness。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records_per_model: 115200\n      total_records: 230400\n      accuracy_qwen14b_bf16: 0.752\n      accuracy_deepseek14b_bf16: 0.738\n      precision_gap_pp_avg: 0.35\n      item_id_pct_qwen14b: 50.5\n      item_id_pct_deepseek14b: 46.8\n      item_id_pct_avg: 48.7\n      prompt_x_item_deepseek14b: 8.2\n      g_coeff_binary_200_avg: 0.35\n      gpu_hours_used: 85\n    result_rationale: >\n      14B 模型的 item_id (~49%) 略低于 8B (~53%)，因为更强的模型对更多 items 有高置信\n      正确答案 (ceiling effect)，压缩了 item 间 accuracy 变异。precision gap 从 ~8pp\n      降到 <0.4pp——14B 模型 logit margin 更大，bf16/fp16 truncation 几乎不翻转预测。\n      DeepSeek-R1-Distill 的 prompt×item 偏高 (8.2%) 可能源于 reasoning-distilled\n      架构对 prompt 格式的条件依赖更强。整体方差结构保持一致，支持跨 scale 泛化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: 8B vs 14B variance structure (MMLU, single-model, binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, \"8B avg\": 52.9, Qwen3_14B: 50.5, DeepSeek_14B: 46.8}\n          - {source: \"prec×item\", \"8B avg\": 7.0, Qwen3_14B: 3.2, DeepSeek_14B: 2.8}\n          - {source: \"prompt×item\", \"8B avg\": 5.6, Qwen3_14B: 5.0, DeepSeek_14B: 8.2}\n          - {source: precision, \"8B avg\": 2.1, Qwen3_14B: 0.2, DeepSeek_14B: 0.15}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: 8B vs 14B item_id comparison bar chart。Scale 增大 item_id 略降但 rank structure 不变。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale robustness 得到确认。14B 的 precision sensitivity 大幅下降 (<0.4pp) 是一个\n      useful practical finding——更大的模型对数值精度更稳健。适合 Appendix/Supplementary。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"Fine-tuning G-study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      RoBERTa-large fine-tuning × SST-2/MNLI/RTE/COPA。6 seeds × 3 LR × 4 data\n      shuffles × 3 GPUs × 2 precisions = 432 runs/task × 4 tasks = 1728 total。\n    expected_results:\n      total_runs: 1728\n      tasks_completed: 4\n      learning_rate_pct: 22.0\n      seed_pct: 18.5\n      data_shuffle_pct: 16.0\n      item_id_pct: 12.5\n      residual_pct: 14.0\n      lr_x_item_pct: 4.8\n      seed_x_item_pct: 5.5\n      data_shuffle_x_item_pct: 3.5\n      gpu_pct: 0.6\n      precision_pct: 0.4\n      gpu_x_precision_pct: 0.2\n      other_pct: 2.0\n      g_coeff_binary_avg: 0.45\n      accuracy_sst2: 0.942\n      accuracy_mnli: 0.876\n      accuracy_rte: 0.728\n      accuracy_copa: 0.685\n      item_id_rank: 4\n      top_source: learning_rate\n      gpu_hours_used: 165\n    result_rationale: >\n      fine-tuning 的方差层级与 inference 根本不同。learning_rate (22%) 主导因为 encoder\n      fine-tuning 在小 LR 范围内对最终性能极敏感 (Dodge et al. 2020)。seed (18.5%) 和\n      data_shuffle (16%) 上升是因为 SGD 随机性在小数据集 (RTE 2.5K, COPA 400 samples)\n      上导致训练轨迹显著分歧——不同 seed 可能收敛到 loss landscape 的不同局部最优。\n      item_id 降到 12.5% 因为 fine-tuning 让模型适应了 task-specific item 难度分布，\n      压缩了 item 间差异。GPU 和 precision 合计 <1%——training 的随机性远超硬件噪声。\n      这个「方差层级翻转」(item_id 从 #1 降到 #4) 表明 inference 和 fine-tuning 需要\n      完全不同的 reproducibility budget。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S2: Inference vs fine-tuning variance hierarchy (%)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: \"item_id / item_id\", inference_MMLU: 52.9, finetuning_avg: 12.5, shift: \"↓41pp (#1→#4)\"}\n          - {source: \"precision / learning_rate\", inference_MMLU: 2.1, finetuning_avg: 22.0, shift: \"↑20pp (不同 facet)\"}\n          - {source: \"seed main / seed main\", inference_MMLU: 0.2, finetuning_avg: 18.5, shift: \"↑18pp\"}\n          - {source: \"prompt / data_shuffle\", inference_MMLU: 0.9, finetuning_avg: 16.0, shift: \"↑15pp (不同 facet)\"}\n          - {source: \"GPU / GPU\", inference_MMLU: \"<0.1\", finetuning_avg: 0.6, shift: \"≈\"}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Paired stacked-bar: inference (MMLU) vs fine-tuning 方差层级。可视化 item_id 和 LR/seed 的位置互换。\"\n      - \"Fig S3: Per-task fine-tuning 方差分解。RTE/COPA (小数据) 的 seed variance 远大于 SST-2/MNLI。\"\n    analysis: >\n      fine-tuning 结果为论文贡献了 scope qualification：item dominance 是 inference\n      evaluation 的特征，不是 ML evaluation 的普遍规律。GPU×precision 在 fine-tuning\n      中也可忽略 (0.2%)，说明 infra separability 跨 paradigm 成立。RTE/COPA 的高 seed\n      variance 与 Dodge et al. (2020) 一致。此实验适合论文 Discussion section 用于\n      界定 claims 的适用范围。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"LayerCast precision study\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007\"\n    description: >\n      LayerCast (fp16 storage + fp32 compute) as 4th precision condition on MMLU。\n      Llama × 4 prec × 3 prompts × 3 seeds × 2 temps × 2 orderings × 200 items。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 28800\n      conditions: 144\n      accuracy_layercast: 0.708\n      accuracy_bf16: 0.711\n      accuracy_fp16: 0.711\n      accuracy_fp32: 0.604\n      layercast_bf16_gap_pp: 0.3\n      layercast_fp32_gap_pp: 10.4\n      precision_variance_with_layercast: 1.4\n      precision_x_item_with_layercast: 4.8\n      precision_variance_without_layercast: 2.1\n      precision_x_item_without_layercast: 7.0\n      gpu_hours_used: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      LayerCast (0.708) 接近 bf16 (0.711) 因为 fp32 compute path 保留了 attention\n      计算精度，fp16 storage 不影响前向传播。与 pure fp32 (0.604) 的 10.4pp 差距证实\n      fp32 degradation 不是数值精度本身的问题，而是 vLLM fp32 code path 的系统差异\n      (可能涉及不同的 attention kernel 或 memory layout)。从 G-theory 角度，加入\n      LayerCast 后 precision 方差分量从 2.1% 降到 1.4%——有改善但不戏剧性，因为\n      fp32 仍然是 outlier。precision×item 从 7.0% 降到 4.8% 说明 LayerCast 减少了\n      item-conditional 精度效应。这提供了 practical mitigation recommendation 但\n      不改变论文核心叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S3: LayerCast vs standard precisions (Llama, MMLU)\"\n        rows:\n          - {precision: LayerCast, accuracy: 0.708, prec_pct: 0.3, prec_x_item_pct: 4.5}\n          - {precision: bf16, accuracy: 0.711, prec_pct: 0.1, prec_x_item_pct: 3.8}\n          - {precision: fp16, accuracy: 0.711, prec_pct: 0.1, prec_x_item_pct: 3.9}\n          - {precision: fp32, accuracy: 0.604, prec_pct: 2.1, prec_x_item_pct: 7.0}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S4: 4-precision accuracy bar chart with LayerCast。LayerCast ≈ bf16 >> fp32。\"\n    analysis: >\n      LayerCast 是 Appendix mitigation recommendation。核心贡献是排除 fp32 degradation\n      的「纯数值精度」解释——fp32 compute 在 LayerCast 中正常工作，问题出在 vLLM fp32\n      engine path。\n\n  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  - name: \"MATH benchmark extension\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      MATH (200 items) × 3 models × 2 prec (bf16/fp16) × 6 prompts × 6 seeds ×\n      2 temps × 4 orderings。测试 chain-of-thought 推理的方差结构。\n    expected_results:\n      total_records: 345600\n      accuracy_avg: 0.285\n      accuracy_llama: 0.312\n      accuracy_qwen: 0.335\n      accuracy_mistral: 0.208\n      # --- single-model G-study (binary, avg) ---\n      item_id_pct: 28.0\n      residual_pct: 26.5\n      seed_x_item_pct: 12.8\n      temp_x_item_pct: 11.5\n      prompt_x_item_pct: 8.2\n      precision_x_item_pct: 1.5\n      seed_pct: 3.2\n      temperature_pct: 3.5\n      precision_x_temp_binary: 0.18\n      other_pct: 4.62\n      # --- model-as-facet (exp-004 extended) ---\n      maf_item_id: 16.0\n      maf_model_x_item: 28.0\n      maf_model: 15.0\n      # --- G-coefficients ---\n      g_coeff_binary_200: 0.18\n      g_coeff_text_match_200: 0.62\n      # --- D-study projection ---\n      dstudy_g90_binary: 950\n      gpu_hours_used: 42\n    result_rationale: >\n      MATH 的 item_id (28% 单模型, 16% model-as-facet) 是所有 benchmarks 中最低的，\n      因为多步数学推理中的 CoT 路径选择引入了巨大的 seed-conditional 和 temp-conditional\n      item 变异。seed×item (12.8%) + temp×item (11.5%) 合计 24.3%——一道题能否做对\n      取决于模型恰好走了哪条推理链，这是高度随机的。residual 高达 26.5% 反映了 CoT\n      的内在不可预测性——大量 item-level 方差无法归因于任何已测量 facet。model-as-facet\n      下 model×item (28%) > item_id (16%)：3 模型的数学能力差异极大 (Qwen 34% vs\n      Mistral 21%)，且不同模型擅长不同类型的数学题 (代数 vs 几何 vs 组合)，创造了\n      强 differential item functioning。precision×temperature 仅 0.18% (binary)\n      因为 bf16/fp16-only 设计——这不构成 separability 的有力测试。G=0.18 是所有\n      benchmark 中最低的，说明 200-item binary 在 MATH 上几乎无信号。D-study 需要\n      ~950 items 达到 G≥0.90，是 MMLU 的 1.5×。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: MATH vs GSM8K vs MMLU (single-model avg, binary, %)\"\n        rows:\n          - {source: item_id, MMLU: 52.9, GSM8K: 34.5, MATH: 28.0}\n          - {source: \"seed×item\", MMLU: 3.1, GSM8K: 11.5, MATH: 12.8}\n          - {source: \"temp×item\", MMLU: 6.4, GSM8K: 10.8, MATH: 11.5}\n          - {source: residual, MMLU: 17.1, GSM8K: 23.8, MATH: 26.5}\n          - {source: G_binary_200, MMLU: 0.33, GSM8K: 0.22, MATH: 0.18}\n      - name: \"Table S5: Extended D-study across 5 benchmarks (items for G≥0.90, binary)\"\n        rows:\n          - {benchmark: HellaSwag, items: 480}\n          - {benchmark: ARC, items: 540}\n          - {benchmark: MMLU, items: 620}\n          - {benchmark: GSM8K, items: 780}\n          - {benchmark: MATH, items: 950}\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S5: Extended 5-benchmark stacked-bar (with MATH)。MATH 作为最极端推理任务，item_id 最低、seed/temp interaction 最高。\"\n      - \"Fig S6: D-study projection curves extended to 5 benchmarks。MATH 曲线最右——需要最多 items。\"\n    analysis: >\n      MATH 延续并强化了 GSM8K 的模式。5-benchmark 梯度 (HellaSwag 51% ≈ MMLU 53% >\n      ARC 44% > GSM8K 35% > MATH 28%, 单模型; HellaSwag 33% ≈ MMLU 35% > ARC 27% >\n      GSM8K 20% > MATH 16%, model-as-facet) 在方向上一致但 HellaSwag≈MMLU 仍然非单调。\n      MATH 的加入使 gradient 叙事更有说服力——从 knowledge retrieval 到 multi-step\n      reasoning 的 item_id 递减跨越 ~20pp (model-as-facet)。D-study 范围扩展到\n      480-950 items (G≥0.90)，differentiation 比只有 4 benchmarks 时更明显。\n      此实验适合 Supplementary 或 extended analysis，强化 Claim 1 和 Claim 3。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"163d87c8-e4af-4d67-b25b-2fbd3a2124ac","total_cost_usd":1.4239770000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13670,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":52955,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":52955,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8634,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008733999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":52955,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13670,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4152430000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"19b7f2a6-49d6-4366-8056-8acda2d4d612"}
